description: Quote revisions are versions of one RFQ, created only on successful delivery
alwaysApply: true
---

# Quote versions (locked spec)

Revisions are **v1 → v2 of the same RFQ**. Do not mint new RFQ ids.

A version is created **only on successful delivery**:

- Member: `quoteRfqToBuyer` (Submit / Update quote to buyer) — still sets `reviewStatus: quoted` and must **not** run for guests.
- Guest: **Quote sent on WhatsApp** (`quoteDelivery: "whatsapp"` only — never `reviewStatus: quoted` via `quoteRfqToBuyer`).

Worksheet edits are **draft** until that send. Effective = last delivered. Dropdown is **view**, not make-effective.

Same version list on portal RFQ detail and marketplace My RFQs. Label `vN` + sent time + **Current** on effective.

Guest WhatsApp then Assign then Submit To Buyer is **one timeline** (WA v1/v2, member submit v3). Do not drop WhatsApp history.

Old version cannot be resent in place — **Load into draft**, then send, which freezes a **new** version. Confirm if the draft is dirty.

PO from a quote only against the **effective** version. A PO can also be created directly from priced goods (`unit_price > 0`) via Buy now, with no quote version. Unpriced goods have no Buy now, only Ask price (RFQ). The quote-version PO rules above are unchanged. Portal old version = read-only preview; edit only on **Draft**. Keep frozen public `/zh/quote/:token` URLs. Do not treat multi-supplier Variant A as versions.

```jsx
// ❌ BAD
<button onClick={() => quoteRfqToBuyer(guestRfq.id)}>Submit To Buyer</button>
setEffective(dropdownValue);

// ✅ GOOD
<button disabled={rfqBuyerKind(rfq) !== "member"}>Submit To Buyer</button>
<select>{/* v1 · datetime · Current — view only */}</select>
<button onClick={loadVersionIntoDraft}>Load into draft</button>
```
